# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.tgz
*.zip

# ── Secrets — never commit ────────────────────────────────────
# rundot CLI credentials live in %USERPROFILE%\.rundot_cli, outside this repo.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
.rundot_cli/
.rundot/

# ── Fetched SDK docs (regenerate: npx rundot-sdk-setup -y) ─────
**/rundot/docs/
**/.rundot-docs

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ── OS / editor cruft ─────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# ── Test / coverage ───────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/

# ── Generation sidecars: keep locally, never publish ──────────
# rundot generate image writes these beside each PNG. They carry the
# prompt, seed, and a storage URL embedding the creator account id.
*.png.json

# ── Supplied audio masters: kept out of git regardless ─────────
# 5 SFX WAVs + an empty BGM folder arrived Sep 4. User confirmed same day
# all five clips are CC0-licensed and need no additional licence, so this
# is no longer a provenance hold — masters just stay out of the repo for
# size, and because the source still isn't named anywhere (including
# LICENSE.txt). Converted, budgeted copies ship from jam-entry/public/audio/
# instead. Plan §7 items 27, 28.
Ramu - The Chef/Audio/

# ── Purchased art packs: must NOT be redistributed ─────────────
# Two commercial itch.io tilesets arrived Sep 4 (toxiccolors "Kitchen
# Inventory Decoration", hoshiixs "Kitchen Props") with .aseprite sources
# and Tiled .tsx/.tsj. This repo is PUBLIC: paid asset packs typically
# license use *inside* a game, not redistribution of the raw sheets, so
# committing these would republish purchased art. Sprites cut from them
# ship as baked atlases under jam-entry/public/images/ instead. Licence
# terms still need reading per pack — Plan §7.
Ramu - The Chef/Art/

# ── Third-party UI pack: must NOT be redistributed ────────
# "Cozy UI Pack" by dobo_ui (itch.io), arrived Sep 7. Its own
# developerNote calls it the DEMO version, which is the tier least
# likely to permit redistribution. Same reasoning as Art/ and Audio/
# above: this repo is PUBLIC. Sprites cut from it ship baked under
# jam-entry/public/images/. Licence terms still need reading.
Ramu - The Chef/UI/

# ── Credentials: NEVER commit ──────────────────────────────────
# Share URLs carry their access key in ?k=. This repo is PUBLIC, so a
# key in a tracked doc is a published key. Created Sep 7 2026 at the
# user's request, deliberately outside version control.
Ramu - The Chef/docs/private build keys.md

# ── Licensed Pixabay audio: must NOT be redistributed ────────
# Three BGM loops (alex morgan) + two SFX one-shots (grumpynora,
# freesound_community), sourced Sep 12 from Pixabay. The Pixabay Content
# Licence permits use *inside* a game but not redistribution of the files
# standalone -- and this repo is PUBLIC, which is exactly that. User's
# position, Sep 12: the third BGM track has no licence file of its own, but
# all three come from the same artist on the same platform, so they are
# treated as the same licence.
#
# These are therefore the first files under jam-entry/public/ deliberately
# left untracked. `rundot deploy` ships dist/, which Vite builds from the
# local public/ folder, so git was never the delivery path. A fresh clone
# builds and runs; it just boots silent until these are restored from
# Ramu - The Chef/Audio/_gen/music-pixabay-final/ and /sfx-pixabay-final/.
jam-entry/public/cdn-assets/bgm-menu.mp3
jam-entry/public/cdn-assets/bgm-service-low.mp3
jam-entry/public/cdn-assets/bgm-service-high.mp3
jam-entry/public/audio/wave-clear-bell.mp3
jam-entry/public/audio/bombay-transition.mp3

# Generated ad creatives (`rundot marketing prepare/generate`). 16 MB of PNGs
# plus prompt/seed sidecars, all regenerable from campaign.json. No secrets --
# the sidecars carry prompt/model/seed only, and campaign.json's gameId is
# already public -- this is excluded as build working material, not as a leak.
jam-entry/rundot/marketing/
